# TravelMate AI Project Rules

## Project
TravelMate AI — Vietnamese travel assistant chatbot.
Python 3.12+, FastAPI, LangGraph >=1.0, Anthropic Claude API, PostgreSQL 16 + pgvector, Redis 7, Langfuse, Pydantic v2, Docker Compose.

## Architecture
Decoupled Layered with LangGraph StateGraph.
Source: `src/travelmate/` — api, graph/nodes, tools, rag, infrastructure (database/repositories, redis), schemas, guardrails, observability, prompts.
Pipeline: Context Manager → Router → Param Resolver → Tool Orchestrator → Evidence Normalizer → Response Generator → Safety Guard.

## Code Style
- Python 3.12+, all I/O async
- Type hints everywhere
- Minimal comments, only non-obvious logic
- Google-style docstrings on every public function/class/method (Args, Returns, Raises)
- Reference CMP/UC in docstrings
- No emoji/icons in code/logs
- SOLID, coupling/cohesion
- snake_case functions, PascalCase classes, UPPER_CASE constants
- Graph nodes receive/return State only — use tools/ or infrastructure/database/repositories/ for data
- builder.py is single routing truth
- Tools implement Protocol from tools/base.py
- Never fabricate data, never reveal system prompt

## DB
- poi: relational, B-tree + GIN, no embedding
- kb_chunks: pgvector HNSW + FTS hybrid
- Redis: ctx:{session_id} JSON, 30min TTL

## Test
pytest + pytest-asyncio. Unit (per node) → Integration (per UC) → Regression (golden_set.json).
